#RBAC with oatuh2_proxy_client authorization

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User (Browser)
    participant N as NGINX (mTLS + auth_request)
    participant O as oauth2-proxy (OIDC session)
    participant R as RBAC Middleware (api.sua-app.com)
    participant DB as RBAC Policy DB (roles/allowlists/limits)
    participant S as Signer/Relayer (KMS)
    participant CH as Chain RPC (node)

    %% ---- PRECONDITION: user is already logged in ----
    note over U,O: Browser holds _oauth2_proxy session cookie (HttpOnly, Secure)

    %% ---- TRANSFER REQUEST FROM THE PORTAL ----
    U->>N: POST /api/transfer  (credentials: include; CSRF header)
    note over N: mTLS: verify client cert (optional but recommended)

    %% ---- AUTHN CHECK AT THE EDGE ----
    N->>O: subrequest /oauth2/auth  (validate session cookie)
    O-->>N: 200 OK + X-Auth-Request-User/Email/Groups
    note over N: If 401 → 302 to /oauth2/start (not shown)

    %% ---- FORWARD TO RBAC WITH IDENTITY CONTEXT ----
    N->>R: Proxy /api/transfer<br/>X-Auth-Request-User, X-Auth-Request-Email, X-SSL-Client-Verify/CN, CSRF token

    %% ---- RBAC AUTHORIZATION ----
    R->>R: Validate CSRF, content-type, schema (amount, from, to, contract)
    R->>DB: Fetch user→tenant mapping, roles, wallet/contract allowlists, tx limits
    DB-->>R: {roles:["writer"], wallets:["0xFrom..."], contracts:["0xToken..."], limits:{daily:..., perTx:...}}
    R->>R: Enforce policy: role=writer? fromWallet allowed? contract allowed? amounts/limits OK?
    alt Authorized
        %% ---- PREP + SUBMIT TRANSACTION ----
        R->>S: Build tx (e.g., ERC20 transfer), EIP-1559 params, optional EIP-712; request signature
        S->>CH: Send signed tx to chain RPC
        CH-->>S: txHash / receipt (pending or mined)
        S-->>R: {txHash, status:pended}
        R-->>N: 200 { txHash, status:"submitted" }
        N-->>U: 200 { txHash, status:"submitted" }
    else Denied
        R-->>N: 403 { error:"not_authorized", reason:"wallet/contract/role/limit" }
        N-->>U: 403 { error, reason }
    end

Browser → NGINX: POST /api/transfer with the session cookie (from oauth2-proxy) and a CSRF header from your SPA.

NGINX → oauth2-proxy: auth_request validates the cookie. If valid, oauth2-proxy returns 200 and injects identity headers (e.g., X-Auth-Request-User, X-Auth-Request-Email, X-Auth-Request-Groups).

NGINX → RBAC: forwards the call, passing the identity headers (and, if you enforce device binding, X-SSL-Client-Verify/X-SSL-Client-CN).

RBAC:

Validates CSRF and the payload (from, to, amount, contractAddress).

Loads roles & allowlists from its Policy DB (e.g., writer role; fromWallet allowed; contract allowed; per-tx/daily limits).

If authorized, RBAC prepares the transaction (ERC-20 transfer or equivalent), optionally as EIP-712 typed data, requests a signature from the Signer/Relayer (KMS), and submits to the Chain RPC. Returns { txHash, status:"submitted" }.

If denied, returns 403 with the reason (role/wallet/contract/limit).





